From e075e1893ab372538a14fed4bb1f5df16ed7e14e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] Noah-MP phasechange: keep the heat of a melted-out snow
 layer

When a snow layer melts out, its leftover heat (heatr) goes to the layer
below as melt. If that layer is below freezing the heat is deleted.

Warm the layer below instead when it is not melting.

Not triggered in the C96 March test case.

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90 b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
index 7eaa43d8..4f2ddadd 100644
--- a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
+++ b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90
@@ -6847,8 +6847,12 @@ zolmax = xkrefsqr / sqrt(xkzo)   ! maximum z/L
                if (mliq(j)*mice(j)>0.) stc(j) = tfrz
                if (mice(j) == 0.) then         ! barlage
                   stc(j) = tfrz                ! barlage
-                  hm(j+1) = hm(j+1) + heatr    ! barlage
-                  xm(j+1) = hm(j+1)*dt/hfus    ! barlage
+                  if (imelt(j+1) > 0) then
+                    hm(j+1) = hm(j+1) + heatr    ! barlage
+                    xm(j+1) = hm(j+1)*dt/hfus    ! barlage
+                  else
+                    stc(j+1) = stc(j+1) + fact(j+1)*heatr  ! layer below not melting: warm it
+                  endif
                endif 
             end if
          endif
